 "script": "Apple's iPhone 18 Pro is expected on September 9.\nAnd if the reports hold, it changes more than any Pro in years, including one that only matters when you have no signal.\nStart with the camera: a mechanical iris on the main lens that physically opens and closes.\nWide open in the dark. Stopped down when you want everything sharp.\nAnalyst Ming-Chi Kuo says that lens alone costs about 50% more.\nBut you'd notice this one more: the Dynamic Island could shrink about 35%, as Face ID's illuminator moves under the display.\nInside, the A20 Pro would be Apple's first 2nm chip: reportedly 15% faster, on 30% less power.\nPair that with a Pro Max battery about 10% bigger.\nBack to that signal.\nApple's own C2 modem reportedly adds 5G over satellite. Coverage with no tower in sight.\nSo this isn't just a camera upgrade.\nThe screen, the chip, the signal, even the frosted back it's wrapped in, reportedly in a new Dark Cherry.\nNone of it is official until Apple says so.\nBut which one would actually make you upgrade?",
 "approval": {
